# Solar Pi — battery packs (JBD/ECO BMS over BLE). One pack per line.
#
# Copy this file to  packs.conf  (in ~/solardash, beside solardash.env) and edit it:
#     cp packs.conf.example packs.conf
# Then restart:  systemctl --user restart solardash
#
# Columns are whitespace-separated:   MAC   [position]   [name]
#   MAC       required. The pack's Bluetooth address (aa:bb:cc:dd:ee:ff).
#   position  optional integer — the "#N" label shown on the tile. Just a label; set it to
#             whatever you want (see the README note about DIP switches vs. displayed position).
#   name      optional. Defaults to the MAC's last 6 hex digits.
# '#' starts a comment; blank lines are ignored.
#
# Tip: don't hand-type MACs — run `python deploy/ble_scan.py --emit` on the Pi and paste the
# output here. That way an 08-vs-0B typo can't happen in the first place.
#
# MAC                  pos  name
# AA:C2:37:06:56:72     1    Pack-1
# AA:C2:37:06:57:4C     2    Pack-2
# AA:C2:37:08:25:3D     3    Pack-3
# AA:C2:37:08:25:44     4    Pack-4
# AA:C2:37:0B:40:05     5    Pack-5
# AA:C2:37:0B:40:6A     6    Pack-6
